          %h2#idea Idea
          %h3#General General
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+supersymmetry"} extended supersymmetry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermultiplets"} supermultiplets
            have some of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetries
            retained (have 0-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eigenvalue"} eigenvalue
            under some of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            generators). These are called
            = succeed "." do
              %strong Bogomol’nyi–Prasad–Sommerfield saturated solutions
          %p
            More in detail, where in a plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
            a suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basis"} basis
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{Q_A\}
            of supersymmetry generators has odd bracket proportional to the spacetime translation and hence to an
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/energy"} energy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
            operator
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            (with terminology as at
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+representation+of+the+Poincar%C3%A9+group"} unitary representation of the Poincaré group
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo =
                  %mi E
                  %msub
                    %mi δ
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\{Q_A, Q_B\} = E \delta_{A B}
          %p
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+supersymmetry"} extended supersymmetry
            there are further bosonic super Lie algebra generators
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_{A B}
            (charges) such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo =
                  %mi E
                  %msub
                    %mi δ
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mi B
                  %mo −
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\{Q_A, Q_B\} = E \delta_{A B} -  K_{A B}
                  \\,.
          %p
            It follows from the supersymmetry algebra that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %msub
                    %mi δ
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mi B
                  %mo −
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E \delta_{A B} -  K_{A B})
            is a positive definite
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+form"} bilinear form
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/energy"} energy
            given the values of these extra charges. This is called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em BPS bound
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bridgeland+stability+condition"} Bridgeland stability condition
          %p
            In particular when this bound is satisfied in that some of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eigenvalues"} eigenvalues
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix"} matrix
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (K_{A B})
            are actually equal to the energy/mass, then the corresponding component of the right hand side in the above equation vanishes and hence then the corresponding supersymmetry generators may annihilate the given state, then called a
            = succeed "." do
              %em BPS state
          %p
            States with similar behaviour are also considered also in some models of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/soliton"} soliton
            theory (English Wikipedia:
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bogomol'nyi%E2%80%93Prasad%E2%80%93Sommerfield_bound"} Bogomol’nyi–Prasad–Sommerfield bound
          %p
            BPS states play a central role in the investigation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+spaces"} moduli spaces
            of classical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacua"} vacua
            as they form part of the moduli problem which is often the most tractable.
          %p
            Several mathematical theories in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            are interpreted as counting BPS-states in the sense of integration on appropriate compactification of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
            of BPS-states in a related physical model attached to the underlying geometry: most notably the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gromov-Witten+invariants"} Gromov-Witten invariants
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Donaldson-Thomas+invariants"} Donaldson-Thomas invariants
            and the
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas-Pandharipande+invariants"} Thomas-Pandharipande invariants
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stability+conditions"} stability conditions
          %h3#in_supergravity In supergravity
          %p
            In the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            BPS states correspond to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+spacetimes"} super spacetimes
            admitting
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Killing+vectors"} Killing vectors
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black brane
            solutions.
          %h3#in_superstring_theory In superstring theory
          %p
            Specifically in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring+theory"} superstring theory
            BPS states in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
            correspond to string states on the worldsheet which are annihilated by the left-moving (say) half of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac-Ramond+operator"} Dirac-Ramond operator
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "Witten+genus#RelationToBPSStateCounting"} Witten genus – Relation to BPS states
          %p
            The degeneracy of BPS states in string theory has been used to provide a microscopic interpretation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bekenstein-Hawking+entropy"} Bekenstein-Hawking entropy
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+holes"} black holes
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+holes+in+string+theory"} black holes in string theory
          %h2#InTermsOfHigherDifferentialGeometry Formalization in higher differential geometry
          %blockquote
            %p
              The following are some observations on the formalization of BPS states from the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nPOV"} nPOV
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#SatiSchreiber15"} Sati &amp; Schreiber 2015
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1|N}
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-Minkowski+spacetime"} super-Minkowski spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mi N
                  %mo ,
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (d,N,p)
            be in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
            and write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo ≔
                  %mover
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∧
                      %mi p
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\phi \coloneqq \bar{\psi} \wedge E^{\wedge p} \wedge \psi \in \Omega^{p+2}(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1|N})
          %p
            for the correspoding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} cocycle
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional"} Green-Schwarz action functional
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#FSS13"} FSS 13
          %p
            Consider then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-spacetime"} super-spacetime
            locally modeled on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1|N}
            as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+geometry"} Cartan geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            (e.g.
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mn 11
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d= 11
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+supergravity"} heterotic supergravity
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo =
                  %mn 10
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 10
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N = (1,0)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+supergravity"} type IIA supergravity
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo =
                  %mn 10
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 10
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N= (1,1)
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIB+supergravity"} type IIB supergravity
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo =
                  %mn 10
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 10
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N= (2,0)
          %p
            This means in particular that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            carries a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+differential+form"} super differential form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\omega \in \Omega^{p+2}(X)
          %p
            which is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definite+form"} definite
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW-term"} WZW-term
            which defines the relevant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-brane+sigma-model"} super p-brane sigma-model
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            By (
            %a{:href => "#AGIT89"}> AGIT 89
            )
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a BPS state to the extent that it carries
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Killing+spinors"} Killing spinors
            which form a central
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+extension"} Lie algebra extension
            of a sub-algebra of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            algebra (i.e. of the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+translation+Lie+algebra"} super translation Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi dR
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^p_{dR}(X)
            which is classified by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} cocycle
            given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi cl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi im
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi d
                    %mi dR
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\epsilon_1, \epsilon_2) \mapsto
                  \\omega(\epsilon_1,\epsilon_2)
                  \\in
                  \\Omega^p(X)_{cl}/im(\mathbf{d}_{dR})
                  \\,.
          %p
            Now we observe that by (
            %a{:href => "#hgpII"}> hgpII, theorem 3.3.1
            ) this is precisely the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-truncation"} 0-truncation
            of the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-infinity+algebra"} super
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+bracket+Lie+n-algebra"} Poisson bracket Lie n-algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔓𝔬𝔦𝔰
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{Pois}(X,\omega)
            induced by regarding
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\omega)
            as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pre-n-plectic+manifold"} pre-n-plectic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
            and restricting along the inclusion of the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Killing+vectors"} Killing vectors
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Killing+spinors"} Killing spinors
            into all the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+vector+fields"} Hamiltonian vector fields
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi dR
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mn 0
                  %mi 𝔓𝔬𝔦𝔰
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Vect
                    %mi Ham
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^p_{dR}(X) \to \tau_0 \mathfrak{Pois}(X,\omega) \to Vect_{Ham}(X)
          %p
            (Here we are using that if an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-type"} n-type
            is an extension of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-type"} 0-type
          %p
            The elements in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi dR
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^p_{dR}(X)
            here are precisely the
            = succeed "-brane" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#AGIT89"} AGIT 89, p. 8
          %p
            Hence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is the more BPS the more odd-graded elements there are in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mn 0
                  %mi 𝔓𝔬𝔦𝔰
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_0 \mathfrak{Pois}(X,\omega)
            (or its restriction to super-isometries). Hence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a 1/2 BPS state of supergravity if the odd dimension of this is half that of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,d|N}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,d|N}
          %p Notice that if
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mrow
                              %mi p
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi Γ
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi conn
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                    %mi L
                                  %mi WZW
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi F
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mi ω
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Ω
                            %mi cl
                            %mrow
                              %mi p
                              %mo +
                              %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  \\mathbf{B}^{p+1} (\mathbb{R}/\Gamma)_{conn}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;  {}^{\mathllap{\mathbf{L}_{WZW}}}\nearrow &amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{F_{(-)}}}
                  \\\
                  X
                  \&amp;\stackrel{\omega}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                  \\mathbf{\Omega}^{p+2}_{cl}
                  }
          %p
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+line+n-bundle"} prequantization
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+term"} WZW term
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔓𝔬𝔦𝔰
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{Pois}(X,\omega)
            is supposed to be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+differentiation"} Lie differentiation
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilizer+group"} stabilizer group
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %mi WZW
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}_{WZW}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantomorphism+n-group"} quantomorphism n-group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi QuantMorph
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %mi WZW
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QuantMorph(\mathbf{L}_{WZW})
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = 0
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = 1
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} dcct
            but clearly should hold generally.)
          %p
            Hence we may regard
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi QuantMorph
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mi WZW
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{QuantMorph}(\mathbf{L}_{WZW})
            (or its restriction to super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometries"}> isometries
            ) as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
            of the brane-charge extended supersymmetry algebra. By the discussion at
            %em
              %a{:href => "conserved+current#InHigherPrequantumGeometry"} conserved current – In higher differential geometry
            this is indeed the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-group"} n-group
            of conserved currents of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mi WZW
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}_{WZW}
            regraded as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+Lagrangian"} local Lagrangian
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#AGIT89"} AGIT 89
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#in_11d_supergravity In 11d Supergravity
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"}> M-theory
            ) there are four kinds of 1/2 BPS states (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            = succeed ")" do
