            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/protection+from+quantum+corrections"} protection from quantum corrections
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+energy+theorem"} positive energy theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enhanced+gauge+symmetry"} enhanced gauge symmetry
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+BPS+charges"} geometry of physics – BPS charges
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+branes"} intersecting branes
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/membrane+triple+junction"} membrane triple junction
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general_2 General
          %p
            The BPS bound derives its name from the discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magnetic+monopoles"} magnetic monopoles
            in 4-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%D0%95.+%D0%91.+%D0%91%D0%BE%D0%B3%D0%BE%D0%BC%D0%BE%D0%BB%D1%8C%D0%BD%D1%8B%D0%B9"}> Е. Б. Богомольный
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Устойчивость классических решений
                %strong 24
                (1976) 449-454
              %p Engl. tanslation:
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Evgeny+B.+Bogomolnyj"}> Evgeny B. Bogomolnyj
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Stability of classical solutions
                %strong 24
                (1976) 449 and Yad. Fiz. 24 (1976) 861-870 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/101280"}> spire:101280
                \&amp;rbrack;
              %p reprinted in:
              %p
                %em> Solitons and Particles
                , World Scientific (1984) 389-394 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/0046"}> doi:10.1142/0046
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Manoj+K.+Prasad"}> Manoj K. Prasad
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Sommerfield"} Charles Sommerfield
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Exact classical solution for ‘t Hooft monopole and the Julia-Zee dyon
                %strong 35
                (1975) 760-762 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.35.760"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.35.760
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The extension of the term “BPS-saturated state” from this case to situations in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            seems to have happened in
          %ul
            %li#Witten95
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              , around (2.5) of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/String+Theory+Dynamics+In+Various+Dimensions"} String Theory Dynamics In Various Dimensions
              %strong 443
              (1995) 85-126 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9503124"}> arXiv:hep-th/9503124
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The original article identifying the role of BPS states in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetric
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+theory"} field theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Olive"} David Olive
              %em Supersymmetry algebras that include topological charges
              (2002) (
              %a{:href => "http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/037026937890357X"}> journal
              )
          %p Exposition and review includes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Neitzke"}> Andrew Neitzke
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em What is a BPS state?
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ma.utexas.edu/users/neitzke/expos/bps-expos.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Dimofte10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tudor+Dimofte"}> Tudor Dimofte
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Refined BPS invariants, Chern-Simons theory, and the quantum dilogarithm
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://thesis.library.caltech.edu/5808/1/DimofteTDofficial.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://thesis.library.caltech.edu/5808/"} web
          %p Further developments:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeffrey+Harvey"}> Jeffrey Harvey
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Greg+Moore"} Greg Moore
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebras, BPS states, and strings
                %strong 463
                (1996) 315-368 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213%2895%2900605-2"}> doi:10.1016/0550-3213%2895%2900605-2
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9510182"} hep-th/9510182
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeffrey+Harvey"}> Jeffrey Harvey
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Greg+Moore"} Greg Moore
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the algebras of BPS states
                %strong 197
                (1998), 489–-519,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s002200050461"} doi
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9609017"} hep-th/9609017
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ali+Chamseddine"}> Ali Chamseddine
                , M. S. Volkov,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Non-abelian BPS monopoles in
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
